description:
**Entity** : Oracle America, Inc.

**Job Duties** : Manage the development and implementation process of a specific company product, involving departmental or cross-functional teams focused on the delivery of new or existing products. Plan and direct schedules and monitor budget. Monitor project(s) from initiation through delivery. Organize interdepartmental activities ensuring completion of project/product on schedule and within budget constraints. Assign and monitor work of systems analysis and program staff, providing technical support and direction. May consult with customers or other departments on project status, proposals, or technical issues, such as software system design or maintenance. May telecommute. (385.38287)

Employer will accept a Master’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field and 6 years of experience in the job offered or in a Program Manager-ProdDev-related occupation.

Position requires:

* Lead end to end program management and effective partnerships with engineering, supply chain, demand planning, sourcing and delivery teams;
* Develop and maintain scalable capacity and demand planning models for data center hardware, to align forecasts with product roadmaps and infrastructure growth targets;
* Drive cross-functional execution for new infrastructure programs, including requirements, material readiness, schedule adherence, and go/no-go gates supporting AI/ML and cloud growth;
* Define inventory planning and transition strategies based on utilization and service targets to reduce excess and obsolete (E&O) while meeting cost and SLA objectives;
* Utilize Six Sigma/Lean principles to develop and standardize new processes, conduct root cause analysis, establish tracking mechanisms and KPIs to measure business outcomes and goals;
